PS4: turn off HiZ in RADV on Liverpool/Gladius (it hangs the GPU).
Tested on a PS4 Pro (Gladius): vkcube hangs with HiZ, runs without it.
Rebased onto Mesa 26.3.0: RADV_DEBUG(instance, NO_HIZ).

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
@@ -2791,7 +2791,10 @@
 
    pdev->force_64_byte_sampled_image = !pdev->use_fmask && pdev->drirc.debug.force_64_byte_sampled_image;
 
-   pdev->use_hiz = !(RADV_DEBUG(instance, NO_HIZ));
+   /* PS4 Liverpool/Gladius: HiZ (HTILE) hangs the gfx ring on the first frame
+    * ("ring gfx timeout"); radeonsi's HiZ works. Same as RADV_DEBUG=nohiz. */
+   pdev->use_hiz = !(RADV_DEBUG(instance, NO_HIZ)) &&
+                   pdev->info.family != CHIP_LIVERPOOL && pdev->info.family != CHIP_GLADIUS;
 
    if (pdev->info.gfx_level == GFX12) {
       const char *gfx12_hiz_wa_str = pdev->drirc.performance.gfx12_hiz_wa;
